{
  "hash": "297f1351233e7c33fcd95777b682d2ef",
  "result": {
    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: Regression Tables\nsubtitle: How to Interpret and Create\ndate: today\ndate-format: long\nfooter: \"[IAFF 6501 Website](https://quant4ia.rocks/)\"\nlogo: images/iaff6501-logo.png\nformat:\n  revealjs:\n    theme: [simple, custom.scss]\n    transition: fade\n    slide-number: true\n    #multiplex: true\n    chalkboard: true\nexecute:\n  echo: false\n  message: false\n  warning: false\n  freeze: auto\n---\n\n\n\n# Interpreting Logistic Regression\n\n## The Model Equation\n\n<br>\n\n$$\\log\\left(\\frac{p}{1-p}\\right) = -1.16 - 0.33 \\times \\text{logGDPpc}$$\n\n## What Are Log-Odds?\n\n<br>\n\n::: {.incremental}\n- Logistic regression coefficients are on the **log-odds** scale\n- The **direction** of the effect is easy to read: positive = more likely, negative = less likely\n- But the **magnitude** is hard to interpret directly\n- We need to transform the coefficients into something more intuitive\n:::\n\n## Odds Ratios\n\n<br>\n\n- **Exponentiate** the coefficient to get the **odds ratio**\n- For each one-unit increase in the predictor, the odds of the outcome are **multiplied** by the odds ratio\n\n$$OR = e^b$$\n\n## Interpreting the Odds Ratio {.smaller}\n\n<br>\n\n$$\\log\\left(\\frac{p}{1-p}\\right) = -1.16 - 0.33 \\times \\text{logGDPpc}$$\n\n<br>\n\n$e^{-0.33} \\approx 0.72$\n\n<br>\n\nFor each one-unit increase in log GDP per capita, the odds of conflict onset are **multiplied by 0.72** — a **28% decrease** in the odds of conflict onset.\n\n## Calculating Odds Ratios in R {.smaller}\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\ntidy(bivariate_model, exponentiate = TRUE) |>\n  select(term, estimate, p.value)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n# A tibble: 2 × 3\n  term           estimate  p.value\n  <chr>             <dbl>    <dbl>\n1 (Intercept)       0.365 1.47e- 2\n2 wbgdppc2011est    0.700 2.31e-12\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Predicted Probabilities by Hand\n\n<br>\n\nProbability of conflict onset for a country with log GDP per capita of 9 (~$8,000):\n\n$$\\log\\left(\\frac{p}{1-p}\\right) = -1.16 - 0.33 \\times 9 = -4.13$$\n\n$$\\frac{p}{1-p} = e^{-4.13} = 0.016 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad p = \\frac{0.016}{1.016} \\approx 0.016$$\n\n## Predicted Probabilities with `marginaleffects`\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-fold=\"true\"}\nprediction_data <- data.frame(wbgdppc2011est = c(6, 7, 8, 9, 10))\npred_results <- predictions(bivariate_model, newdata = prediction_data)\n\ntidy(pred_results) |>\n  select(wbgdppc2011est, estimate, conf.low, conf.high) |>\n  mutate(GDP_approx = paste0(\"~$\", round(exp(wbgdppc2011est))))\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n# A tibble: 5 × 5\n  wbgdppc2011est estimate conf.low conf.high GDP_approx\n           <dbl>    <dbl>    <dbl>     <dbl> <chr>     \n1              6   0.0411  0.0322     0.0525 ~$403     \n2              7   0.0291  0.0242     0.0351 ~$1097    \n3              8   0.0206  0.0175     0.0242 ~$2981    \n4              9   0.0145  0.0119     0.0176 ~$8103    \n5             10   0.0102  0.00784    0.0132 ~$22026   \n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Visualizing Predicted Probabilities\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-fold=\"true\" code-summary=\"Show the code\"}\nplot_predictions(bivariate_model, condition = \"wbgdppc2011est\") +\n  labs(\n    title = \"Predicted Probability of Conflict Onset\",\n    x = \"Log GDP per capita\",\n    y = \"Pr(Conflict Onset)\"\n  ) +\n  theme_minimal()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n![](week-6.2_files/figure-revealjs/plot_predictions-1.png){width=960}\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Your Turn! {.smaller}\n\n<br>\n\n- Run a bivariate logistic regression with a different predictor (`v2x_polyarchy`, `ethfrac`)\n- Use `tidy(..., exponentiate = TRUE)` to get the odds ratio\n- Is the effect positive or negative?\n- How much do the odds of conflict onset change per unit increase?\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<countdown-timer class=\"countdown\" id=\"timer-odds\" minutes=\"10\" seconds=\"0\" update-every=\"1\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"right:10%;bottom:5%;--countdown-color-border:#fff;--countdown-color-text:#fff;--countdown-color-running-background:#42affa;--countdown-color-running-text:black;--countdown-color-finished-background:#E5D19D;--countdown-color-finished-text:#00264A;\"></countdown-timer>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n# Multiple Logistic Regression\n\n## Multiple Logistic Regression\n\n<br>\n\n::: {.incremental}\n- Just as with linear models, we can also run multiple logistic regressions\n- We can include multiple predictors in the model\n- Usually we want to include our main predictor of interest and control variables\n- The interpretation of the coefficients is the same as in the bivariate models\n:::\n\n## \n\n<br>\n\nDownload the data using the `peacesciencer` package if you haven't already...\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nconflict_df <- create_stateyears(system = 'gw') |>\n  filter(year %in% c(1946:1999)) |>\n  add_ucdp_acd(type=c(\"intrastate\"), only_wars = FALSE) |>\n  add_democracy() |>\n  add_creg_fractionalization() |>\n  add_sdp_gdp() |>\n  add_rugged_terrain()\n```\n:::\n\n\n## \n\n<br>\n\nExample, including multiple predictors associated with conflict:\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nconflict_model <- glm(ucdponset ~ ethfrac + relfrac + v2x_polyarchy + \n                          rugged + wbgdppc2011est + wbpopest,\n                  data= conflict_df,\n                  family = \"binomial\")\n\nsummary(conflict_model)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n\nCall:\nglm(formula = ucdponset ~ ethfrac + relfrac + v2x_polyarchy + \n    rugged + wbgdppc2011est + wbpopest, family = \"binomial\", \n    data = conflict_df)\n\nCoefficients:\n               Estimate Std. Error z value Pr(>|z|)    \n(Intercept)    -5.37638    1.41017  -3.813 0.000138 ***\nethfrac         0.70870    0.37172   1.907 0.056582 .  \nrelfrac        -0.28760    0.40945  -0.702 0.482425    \nv2x_polyarchy  -0.65166    0.51253  -1.271 0.203563    \nrugged          0.08359    0.07564   1.105 0.269145    \nwbgdppc2011est -0.39172    0.12001  -3.264 0.001099 ** \nwbpopest        0.28469    0.06774   4.203 2.63e-05 ***\n---\nSignif. codes:  0 '***' 0.001 '**' 0.01 '*' 0.05 '.' 0.1 ' ' 1\n\n(Dispersion parameter for binomial family taken to be 1)\n\n    Null deviance: 1205.0  on 6128  degrees of freedom\nResidual deviance: 1147.9  on 6122  degrees of freedom\n  (1495 observations deleted due to missingness)\nAIC: 1161.9\n\nNumber of Fisher Scoring iterations: 7\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Predicted Probabilities\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code  code-fold=\"true\" code-summary=\"Show the code\"}\n# select some countries for a given year\nselected_countries <- conflict_df |>\n  filter(\n    gw_name %in% c(\"United States of America\", \"Venezuela\", \"Rwanda\"),\n    year == 1999)\n\n# calculate margins for the subset\nmarg_effects <- predictions(conflict_model, newdata = selected_countries)\n\n# tidy the results\nlibrary(broom)\n\ntidy(marg_effects) |>\n  select(gw_name, estimate, p.value, conf.low, conf.high) \n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}\n\n```\n# A tibble: 3 × 5\n  gw_name                  estimate  p.value conf.low conf.high\n  <chr>                       <dbl>    <dbl>    <dbl>     <dbl>\n1 United States of America   0.0115 1.63e-28  0.00527    0.0250\n2 Venezuela                  0.0136 1.88e-79  0.00876    0.0211\n3 Rwanda                     0.0331 3.17e-38  0.0201     0.0541\n```\n\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n## Your Turn! \n\n<br>\n\n- Run a multivariate logistic model using conflict onset as the outcome variable\n- Select alternative variables and/or alternative measures of the same variables\n- Interpret some of the coefficients \n- Calculate the predicted probability in a handful of country-years based on your analysis\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<countdown-timer class=\"countdown\" id=\"timer1\" minutes=\"10\" seconds=\"0\" update-every=\"1\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"right:10%;bottom:5%;--countdown-color-border:#fff;--countdown-color-text:#fff;--countdown-color-running-background:#42affa;--countdown-color-running-text:black;--countdown-color-finished-background:#E5D19D;--countdown-color-finished-text:#00264A;\"></countdown-timer>\n```\n\n:::\n:::\n\n\n# Regression Tables\n\n## What's in a Regression Table?\n\n![](images/fearon_laitin.png){fig-align=center}\n\n## Regression Tables with `modelsummary`\n\n<br>\n\n::: {.incremental}\n- Oftentimes we want to show multiple models at once (like F&L)\n- We want to compare across them and see which is the best model\n- How can we do that? \n- There are **many** ways to do this in R\n- We will use the `modelsummary` package\n:::\n\n## Run Multiple Models\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nethnicity <- glm(ucdponset ~ ethfrac + relfrac + wbgdppc2011est + wbpopest, # store each model in an object\n                  data = conflict_df,\n                  family = \"binomial\")\n\ndemocracy <- glm(ucdponset ~ v2x_polyarchy + wbgdppc2011est +  wbpopest,\n                  data = conflict_df,\n                  family = \"binomial\")\n\nterrain <- glm(ucdponset ~ rugged + wbgdppc2011est + wbpopest ,\n                  data = conflict_df,\n                  family = \"binomial\")\n\nfull_model <- glm(ucdponset ~ ethfrac + relfrac + v2x_polyarchy + rugged +\n                        wbgdppc2011est + wbpopest,\n                  data = conflict_df,\n                  family = \"binomial\")\n```\n:::\n\n\n\n## Prep Data for Display\n\n<br>\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nmodels <- list(\"Ethnicity\" = ethnicity,  # store list of models in an object\n               \"Democracy\" = democracy, \n               \"Terrain\" = terrain, \n               \"Full Model\" = full_model)\n\ncoef_map <- c(\"ethfrac\" = \"Ethnic Frac\",  # map coefficients\n        \"relfrac\" = \"Religions Frac\",     #(change names and order)\n        \"v2x_polyarchy\" = \"Polyarchy\",\n        \"rugged\" = \"Terrain\",\n        \"wbgdppc2011est\" = \"Per capita GDP\",\n        \"wbpopest\" = \"Population\",\n        \"(Intercept)\" = \"Intercept\")\n\ncaption = \"Table 1: Predictors of Conflict Onset\" # store caption\nreference = \"See appendix for data sources.\"      # store reference notes\n```\n:::\n\n\n## Display the Models {.smaller}\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<!-- preamble start -->\n\n    <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.js\"></script>\n\n    <script>\n      // Create table-specific functions using external factory\n      const tableFns_q06f74vc0tvgg3hwx0xf = TinyTable.createTableFunctions(\"tinytable_q06f74vc0tvgg3hwx0xf\");\n      // tinytable span after\n      window.addEventListener('load', function () {\n          var cellsToStyle = [\n            // tinytable style arrays after\n          { positions: [ { i: '15', j: 2 }, { i: '15', j: 3 }, { i: '15', j: 4 }, { i: '15', j: 5 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_g0qhkivo1jwvbgvd4b1l',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '14', j: 2 }, { i: '14', j: 3 }, { i: '14', j: 4 }, { i: '14', j: 5 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_s6mxpgi8yojie141z6tk',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '1', j: 2 }, { i: '2', j: 2 }, { i: '3', j: 2 }, { i: '4', j: 2 }, { i: '5', j: 2 }, { i: '6', j: 2 }, { i: '7', j: 2 }, { i: '8', j: 2 }, { i: '9', j: 2 }, { i: '10', j: 2 }, { i: '11', j: 2 }, { i: '12', j: 2 }, { i: '13', j: 2 }, { i: '1', j: 3 }, { i: '2', j: 3 }, { i: '3', j: 3 }, { i: '4', j: 3 }, { i: '5', j: 3 }, { i: '6', j: 3 }, { i: '7', j: 3 }, { i: '8', j: 3 }, { i: '9', j: 3 }, { i: '10', j: 3 }, { i: '11', j: 3 }, { i: '12', j: 3 }, { i: '13', j: 3 }, { i: '1', j: 4 }, { i: '2', j: 4 }, { i: '3', j: 4 }, { i: '4', j: 4 }, { i: '5', j: 4 }, { i: '6', j: 4 }, { i: '7', j: 4 }, { i: '8', j: 4 }, { i: '9', j: 4 }, { i: '10', j: 4 }, { i: '11', j: 4 }, { i: '12', j: 4 }, { i: '13', j: 4 }, { i: '1', j: 5 }, { i: '2', j: 5 }, { i: '3', j: 5 }, { i: '4', j: 5 }, { i: '5', j: 5 }, { i: '6', j: 5 }, { i: '7', j: 5 }, { i: '8', j: 5 }, { i: '9', j: 5 }, { i: '10', j: 5 }, { i: '11', j: 5 }, { i: '12', j: 5 }, { i: '13', j: 5 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_x5299ur07izaxahfm70k',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '0', j: 2 }, { i: '0', j: 3 }, { i: '0', j: 4 }, { i: '0', j: 5 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_yylybuxifnqatg0pppwf',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '15', j: 1 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_kqnx49e1uby87bqsb1m7',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '14', j: 1 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_ksmr634zpip6j2jil8go',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '1', j: 1 }, { i: '2', j: 1 }, { i: '3', j: 1 }, { i: '4', j: 1 }, { i: '5', j: 1 }, { i: '6', j: 1 }, { i: '7', j: 1 }, { i: '8', j: 1 }, { i: '9', j: 1 }, { i: '10', j: 1 }, { i: '11', j: 1 }, { i: '12', j: 1 }, { i: '13', j: 1 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_bmlw9gxu2ecec757lhkb',}, \n          { positions: [ { i: '0', j: 1 } ], css_id: 'tinytable_css_n774tf1yxff9pzhnbaj1',}, \n          ];\n\n          // Loop over the arrays to style the cells\n          cellsToStyle.forEach(function (group) {\n              group.positions.forEach(function (cell) {\n                  tableFns_q06f74vc0tvgg3hwx0xf.styleCell(cell.i, cell.j, group.css_id);\n              });\n          });\n      });\n    </script>\n\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/vincentarelbundock/tinytable@main/inst/tinytable.css\">\n    <style>\n    /* tinytable css entries after */\n    #tinytable_q06f74vc0tvgg3hwx0xf td.tinytable_css_g0qhkivo1jwvbgvd4b1l, #tinytable_q06f74vc0tvgg3hwx0xf th.tinytable_css_g0qhkivo1jwvbgvd4b1l {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 0; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.1em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.1em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%; ; text-align: center }\n    #tinytable_q06f74vc0tvgg3hwx0xf td.tinytable_css_s6mxpgi8yojie141z6tk, #tinytable_q06f74vc0tvgg3hwx0xf th.tinytable_css_s6mxpgi8yojie141z6tk {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 0; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.05em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.1em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%; ; text-align: center }\n    #tinytable_q06f74vc0tvgg3hwx0xf td.tinytable_css_x5299ur07izaxahfm70k, #tinytable_q06f74vc0tvgg3hwx0xf th.tinytable_css_x5299ur07izaxahfm70k { text-align: center }\n    #tinytable_q06f74vc0tvgg3hwx0xf td.tinytable_css_yylybuxifnqatg0pppwf, #tinytable_q06f74vc0tvgg3hwx0xf th.tinytable_css_yylybuxifnqatg0pppwf {  position: relative; --border-bottom: 1; --border-left: 0; --border-right: 0; --border-top: 1; --line-color-bottom: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-left: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-right: var(--tt-line-color); --line-color-top: var(--tt-line-color); --line-width-bottom: 0.05em; --line-width-left: 0.1em; --line-width-right: 0.1em; --line-width-top: 0.1em; --trim-bottom-left: 0%; --trim-bottom-right: 0%; --trim-left-bottom: 0%; --trim-left-top: 0%; --trim-right-bottom: 0%; --trim-right-top: 0%; --trim-top-left: 0%; --trim-top-right: 0%; ; text-align: center }\n    #tinytable_q06f74vc0tvgg3hwx0xf td.tinytable_css_kqnx49e1uby87bqsb1m7, #tinytable_q06f74vc0tvgg3h